```python
def __repr__(self):
    if "base64" in self.url:
        len_base64 = len(self.url.split("base64,")[1])
        image_type = self.url.split(";")[0].split("/")[-1]
        return f"Image(url=data:image/{image_type};base64,<IMAGE_BASE_64_ENCODED({str(len_base64)})>)"
    return f"Image(url='{self.url}')"
```

It reconstructs `data:image/{type}` — for `application/pdf`, `split(";")[0].split("/")[-1]` = "pdf", so repr says `data:image/pdf` — which is wrong MIME (just a display artifact of repr, the actual url is still `data:application/pdf;base64,...`).

